Patches against upstream FireSim (tag 1.21.0) required to build and run a
FireSim simulator on the Alveo U55C under Vitis/Vivado 2024.2.

The paths in these patches are relative to the Vortex repository root, where
the FireSim clone sits at build_firesim/firesim/. Applying them from the root
of a FireSim checkout therefore strips two components, not one:

    cd <firesim>
    patch -p2 < 0001-rebase-target-cycle-counter.patch
    patch -p2 < 0002-vitis-u55c-build-fixes.patch
    patch -p2 < 0003-vitis-memcheck-and-buffer-lifetime.patch
    patch -p2 < 0004-vitis-host-mem-base-address.patch
    patch -p2 < 0005-inflight-target-cycle.patch
    patch -p2 < 0006-package-design-sources.patch
    patch -p2 < 0007-vitis-target-dram-aperture.patch
    patch -p2 < 0008-driver-teardown-before-exit.patch

Apply in order: 0003 and 0005 both touch simulation.{h,cc} and assume 0001 is
already in. Applying the series in order to a pristine 1.21.0 checkout
reproduces this tree's clone byte-for-byte.

0001-rebase-target-cycle-counter.patch
    Correctness fix. The target-cycle counter lives in FPGA fabric and
    persists while the bitstream stays programmed, but simulation_t reported
    it as an absolute value. Every driver invocation against a resident
    xclbin therefore inherited the previous run's count -- observed as
    13, 26, 39, ... cycles of drift across successive runs of the same test,
    with FMR and Effective Target Frequency corrupted alongside it. Host
    cycles were already rebased in the same function; target cycles now are
    too. Host-side only, no bitstream rebuild needed.

0002-vitis-u55c-build-fixes.patch
    Build-flow fixes. Upstream's Vitis flow targets Vitis 2022.1 and a U250;
    neither assumption holds here. See the patch header for the four
    independent failures and their causes.

0003-vitis-memcheck-and-buffer-lifetime.patch
    Correctness fix plus the diagnostic that settled the FASED-on-HBM
    question. The xrt::bo backing host_mem_0 was a constructor local, so its
    device allocation was freed before the simulation ran. +memcheck
    round-trips a pattern through the LoadMem widget before target execution,
    isolating the target DRAM path from the design under test; on the U55C it
    reports an address-independent constant, unchanged by zeroing DRAM --
    i.e. the HBM memory path never accesses memory, while the MMIO/control
    plane is fully functional. See
    docs/proposals/firesim_vitis_host_mem_offset.md.

0004-vitis-host-mem-base-address.patch
    The fix that makes FASED work on an HBM part. VitisShim added a literal
    0x4000000000 (U250 DDR[0] base) to every host_mem_0 address in RTL. On the
    U55C, host_mem_0 binds to HBM[0] at 0x0 with a 512 MB aperture, so every
    access landed outside the window: reads returned a fixed bus default
    independent of address, writes were dropped, and the target DRAM path was
    dead while the control plane still worked. Now a documented constant in
    VitisConstants. Validated with +memcheck under hw_emu: 5/5 probes fail
    before, 0/5 after.

0005-inflight-target-cycle.patch
    Correctness fix on top of 0001. The clock bridge counts target cycles
    *started*, so one cycle is always in flight; it cancels between the two
    samples except across the counter's origin, leaving the first run after
    programming one cycle longer than every run after it (14 vs 13 for a test
    that provably steps 13 times). A fresh metasim is always the origin case,
    so upstream reports the +1 on every metasim run. See
    docs/proposals/firesim_inflight_target_cycle.md.

0006-package-design-sources.patch
    Build-flow fix. A design whose RTL is resolved by library search in
    simulation loses its submodules under Vivado, which has no equivalent.
    VORTEX_VIVADO_SRCS names a flattened source list to add to the packaged
    kernel; absent it the flow is unchanged.

0007-vitis-target-dram-aperture.patch
    Correctness fix. host_mem_0 was bound to a single HBM pseudo-channel and
    backed by a 512 MB allocation, while a 32-bit target spans 4 GB -- its
    program image sits at 0x80000000 and its stack just under 4 GB. Uploading a
    kernel therefore wrote outside the served window and the target fetched
    memory that was never written, with no error anywhere to say so. Widened to
    HBM[0:7] plus a matching 4 GiB window; the two are a pair and each carries a
    comment saying widening one alone truncates silently. The buffer is now
    allocated from whichever memory region can hold the window rather than from
    bank 0 -- a range binding appears as a memory *group* (MBG[0:7], index 39 on
    this platform) whose index cannot be derived from the port name, and
    xrt::ip exposes no group_id(). +memcheck gains probes at 0x20000000,
    0x80000000 and 0xFFFF0000; it passed throughout this defect because it only
    probed below 1 MB, which is how the bug reached the card. No Chisel change:
    HostMemChannelKey.size is already 16 GiB, so the shim's address path was
    never the constraint. See docs/proposals/firesim_target_memory_aperture.md.

0008-driver-teardown-before-exit.patch
    Correctness fix. `simulator` is a global std::unique_ptr, so the platform
    interface was destroyed during static destruction -- and on Vitis that runs
    xrt::device::~device() after XRT's own statics are gone, segfaulting in the
    device registry's deleter. Upstream's comment says the global "must exist
    for dpi.cc calls in emulation, must be global to avoid deletion", but a
    global unique_ptr *is* deleted at exit; nothing references it once entry()
    returns, on either platform. Now torn down explicitly at the end of entry().
    Never observed before because no run had ever reached normal process exit --
    every earlier one timed out.

All are candidates for upstreaming: only the HOST_MEM_SP default is
U55C-specific, and it is parameterized rather than hardcoded. 0005 changes a
reported number relative to upstream; the patch header records why the new
number is the correct one.
